Let $0\leqslant t\leqslant r$ be the largest integer such that there exists a graph in $U(a,j)$ containing $H_t$.
Denote the maximal graph in $(U(a, j)$ by $G$. (Recall that by Lemma~7.1, $G$ contains $H_t$.) 
Let $G'$ be the graph with vertices $P_v$, $v \in \mathbb Z / n \mathbb Z$ 
obtained from $G$ by removing the edges $e_{\pm 1}, \ldots, e_{\pm t}$, i.e., by removing the edges which occur in $H_t$.
Then $G'\in U(a,j,I_t)$.

